{"name":"Komodo","hex":"#a06814","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Komodo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An island of Indonesia, part of the Lesser Sunda Islands"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Komodo dragon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Komodo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Komodo (island)","blocks":[{"text":"Komodo is one of the 17,508 islands that comprise the Republic of Indonesia. It is particularly notable as the habitat of the Komodo dragon, the largest lizard on Earth, which is named after the island. Komodo Island has a surface area of 291 square kilometres, and had a human population of about 1,800 in 2020."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Komodo_Island_north_aerial.jpg/330px-Komodo_Island_north_aerial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Komodo_(island)","wikidata":"Q107640"},{"title":"Komodo (village)","blocks":[{"text":"Komodo is a village on the island of Komodo in Komodo District, West Manggarai Regency, East Nusa Tenggara Province, Indonesia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Komodo_Village.jpg/330px-Komodo_Village.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Komodo_(village)","wikidata":"Q55616153"},{"title":"Komodo (chess)","blocks":[{"text":"Komodo and Dragon by Komodo Chess are UCI chess engines developed by Komodo Chess, which is a part of Chess.com. The engines were originally authored by Don Dailey and GM Larry Kaufman. Dragon is a commercial chess engine, but Komodo is free for non-commercial use. Dragon is consistently ranked near the top of most major chess engine rating lists, along with Stockfish and Leela Chess Zero."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Chess_Programming.svg/330px-Chess_Programming.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_